+    Reconstruct the regional (halo) mesh from neighbouring processor meshes.
+
+    OF-13 PORT (2026-08-19): the upstream implementation stitched the
+    processor meshes with the geometric faceCoupleInfo constructor
+    (mesh, mesh, tol, perfectMatch), which was removed in OpenFOAM-13
+    (only the explicit-addressing constructor remains).  This port finds
+    the coupled boundary-face pairs itself by merging boundary-face
+    centres (Foam::mergePoints) and hands the matched addressing to the
+    remaining constructor.  This is valid because the halo faces are
+    processor-boundary faces of one and the same decomposed mesh: their
+    point coordinates are bitwise identical and decomposePar stores the
+    neighbour-side face as the reversed owner face with the zero-point
+    preserved -- exactly the ordering contract the explicit-addressing
+    faceCoupleInfo requires.
+
+    The upstream file-reading fallback (localPath/readHeader/readFaceList/
+    fileHandlerControl) was deprecated upstream and is not ported: all
+    mesh data travels via Pstream.
 
